      <p class="tm-kind">About this map</p>
      <h2 id="tm-about-title">How to read it</h2>
      <p>This is the map behind Taua, a grand-strategy game I'm building about Aotearoa in 1810. It shows the world the game opens on: who held each place, roughly where hapū territories ran, what covered the land, and the landmarks and tracks that shaped movement.</p>
      <p><b>It is shared for academic review, not for wider publication.</b> Please don't reproduce it. It is working research, built from published sources: Waitangi Tribunal reports, the Dictionary of New Zealand Biography, Te Ara, Crosby's <i>The Musket Wars</i>, Kelly's <i>Tainui</i>, Taylor's <i>Lore and History of the South Island Maori</i>, Native Land Court minutes, the LINZ gazetteer and others, cited place by place.</p>
      <h3>What the marks mean</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Unconfirmed</b> (dashed amber edge): the 1810 holder is a reasoned inference, often from neighbouring places, and still needs a source.</li>
        <li><b>Approximate location</b> (faded): the source names the place but not exactly where it sat.</li>
        <li><b>Placeholder site</b>: a place the game needs whose identity is still being researched.</li>
        <li><b>Consult</b> (red edge on a landmark): a site of particular significance. It won't be modelled without the agreement of the hapū who hold its kōrero.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Limits</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The map is drawn in the game's own space, which is warped from true geography. Don't measure distances or take positions from it.</li>
        <li>Territories are modelled. Each block of land follows the 1810 holder of its nearest place. They are not boundary claims.</li>
        <li>Populations are model estimates, and the plant cover is reconstructed from potential vegetation and early maps.</li>
        <li>Wrong is worse than blank, so where the sources say nothing, the map leaves a gap.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you hold kōrero about a place, or see something wrong, I'd be grateful to hear from you: <a href="mailto:brewer.lewis@gmail.com?subject=Taua%20map">brewer.lewis@gmail.com</a>.</p>
      <p class="tm-fine">Data exported <span id="tm-stamp"></span>. <span id="tm-counts"></span>. Base map built from LINZ Topo50 data (CC BY 4.0) and Manaaki Whenua Landcare Research potential vegetation.</p>
    </div>
